    },
    {
      "filename": "A colourful array of canoes on the banks of the inlet from Lake Ontario (27621372600).jpg",
      "title": "File:A colourful array of canoes on the banks of the inlet from Lake Ontario (27621372600).jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d5/A_colourful_array_of_canoes_on_the_banks_of_the_inlet_from_Lake_Ontario_%2827621372600%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_colourful_array_of_canoes_on_the_banks_of_the_inlet_from_Lake_Ontario_(27621372600).jpg",
      "width": 4928,
      "height": 3264,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0",
      "artist": "shankar s. from Dubai, united arab emirates",
      "description": "A colourful array of canoes stacked upside down on the banks of an inlet which comes in from Lake Ontario (which is just beyond). The blue canoe at the far end bears the name of the club (Toronto Island Canoe Club). According to their website, Toronto Island Canoe Club is a non-profit organization dedicated to promoting the sport of sprint canoe/kayak and to providing opportunities for youth and adults to learn about water safety, develop small boat skills and enjoy the lagoons of Toronto Island. (Toronto, Canada, Nov.2015)",
